{"_v":1,"id":"six-the-musical-west-end-2021","bd":{"positive":8,"mixed":4,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Fiona Mountford","o":"Evening Standard","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/six-the-musical-review-kick-ass-musical-about-henry-viiis-wives-channels-its-inner-beyonce-a3927931.html","d":"2018-09-05","q":"This is quite the most uplifting piece of new British musical theatre I have ever had the privilege to watch"},{"cn":"Marianka Swain","o":"The Telegraph","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/six-the-musical-vaudeville-theatre-review-henry-viii/","d":"2023-11-11","q":"Moss and Jamie Armitage’s infectiously fun production is packed with witty touches that make history, and theatre, easily accessible."},{"cn":"Lyn Gardner","o":"The Guardian","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2018/jan/10/six-review-henry-viii-wives-arts-theatre-london","d":"2018-01-10","q":"It may be cloaked in silliness, but Six makes some serious points about female victimhood and survival."},{"cn":"Marianka Swain","o":"London Theatre","s":94,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/six-review-vaudeville-theatre","d":"2021-11-11","q":"You'd need a heart of stone to resist."},{"cn":"Daisy Bowie-Sell","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/london-theatre/reviews/six-arts-theatre-review_47499.html","d":"2018-09-03","q":"This is a madcap, frenetic, hugely entertaining history remix."},{"cn":"Ava Wong Davies","o":"The Independent","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/six-the-musical-lyric-theatre-review-b1772228.html","d":"2020-12-13","q":"Iconic? Yes, absolutely – just in more ways than one."},{"cn":"Mark Shenton","o":"The Stage","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/six-review-at-arts-theatre-london--raw-talent-and-powerful-voices","d":"2018-01-16","q":"There's undoubtedly raw talent on display in the writing, and really accomplished vocal performances – but it currently feels undernourished and overlong."},{"cn":"Holly Williams","o":"Time Out London","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/six-the-musical-review","d":"2019-01-17","q":"But if this is the future of feminism, lop my head off now."},{"cn":"Amy Rye","o":"Lost in Theatreland","s":95,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://lostintheatreland.co.uk/six-review-vaudeville-theatre/","d":"2024-02-03","q":"This is a unique, exciting, and fun show that can be consumed repeatedly."},{"cn":"Greg Stewart","o":"Theatre Weekly","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theatreweekly.com/review-six-the-musical-2023-cast-at-the-vaudeville/","d":"2023-01-10","q":"Indeed, no matter how many of the previous casts you’ve seen, this is the line-up you don’t want to miss."},{"cn":"Tim Todd","o":"Tim Talks Theatre","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://timtalkstheatre.co.uk/six-the-musical-one-of-a-kind-no-category-my-review/","d":"2024-05-18","q":"If you are looking for a highly entertaining, music filled night at the theatre I would 100% recommend this show to you."},{"cn":"Theatre Bee (UK)","o":"Theatre Bee","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.theatrebee.com/post/review-six","d":"2022-05-19","q":"Catchy music, funny jokes, but an ultimately forgettable performance."}],"au":{"score":90,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"mz":{"s":90,"c":5846,"sr":4.5}}},"hi":"https://images.ctfassets.net/6pezt69ih962/Py6AKCMtiqYKoBSsAmHfc/0343ade4e160de5c7dd4ad91dc82bc7c/SIX25016_TodayTix_1440x580pxls.jpg?fm=webp&q=90","ca":[{"n":"Nia Stephen","r":"Catherine of Aragon"},{"n":"Marisha Morgan","r":"Anne Boleyn"},{"n":"Jessica Aubrey","r":"Jane Seymour"},{"n":"Freya Karlettis","r":"Anna of Cleves"},{"n":"Leesa Tulley","r":"Katherine Howard"},{"n":"Nia Stephen","r":"Catherine Parr"},{"n":"Jarnéia Richard-Noel","r":"Catherine of Aragon"},{"n":"Millie O'Connell","r":"Anne Bol